<title>FRANCE: EU sells German intervention barley, rye.</title>
<headline>EU sells German intervention barley, rye.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday sold 32,786 tonnes of German intervention barley at a minimum price of 104.01 Ecus per tonne for export to countries outside the EU, member country officials said.</p>
<p>The EU's cereals management committtee in Brussels also sold 51,096 tonnes of German intervention rye at a minimum price of 102.52 Ecus per tonne, they said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
